# Owner review for the files that decide whether a merge means anything.
#
# ADR-002 § "Branch protection and rulesets" item 7 requires CODEOWNERS over
# workflows, gate scripts and the required-check manifest; ADR-002 § Contracts
# makes the API contract vizra-core's to change, not this repository's.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE DOES ON ITS OWN: nothing. GitHub enforces it only when a
# ruleset on `main` requires review from Code Owners. Applying that ruleset is
# an owner action and is NOT part of any pull request — see the PR body and
# ADR-002 items 9–10 (which also say no ledger entry may reach VERIFIED on CI
# evidence alone until protection is confirmed applied).
#
# Committing it anyway is deliberate: the file is the reviewable half, it is
# what the ruleset will point at, and `scripts/ci/check-required-floor.sh`
# already enforces the part that needs no repository settings at all.

# Everything, by default, so a new path is not silently unowned.
*                       @yegamble

# CI: the workflows, the fan-in, the required-check manifest and the floor that
# stops the manifest being emptied by the pull request it gates.
/.github/               @yegamble
/scripts/ci/            @yegamble

# The ADR-003 identity and caching lint rules. Two reviewers defeated the first
# version of these; a change here is a change to a privacy control.
/eslint-rules/          @yegamble

# The browser harness. `e2e/harness/` is the default-deny guard, the coverage
# floor and the production-build markers that every later UI slice's evidence
# depends on; weakening one of them would make every subsequent green run mean
# less, with no visible change to any product file.
/e2e/harness/          @yegamble
/playwright.config.ts  @yegamble

# The specs themselves. An independent verifier put one line into e2e/specs/
# that opted a spec out of the browser-error guard entirely, and the whole gate
# went green on a page that 404s and throws. `vizra/no-unguarded-playwright-import`
# now refuses that at lint time — and this line makes a spec that tries anyway,
# or a spec DELETED to slip under the coverage floor, an owner-reviewed diff.
# Every later UI slice adds its specs here.
/e2e/specs/            @yegamble
/e2e/demos/            @yegamble

# The vendored copy of vizra-core's OpenAPI contract and its provenance
# manifest. Editing these here instead of re-vendoring is how a stale or
# hostile contract would enter the build.
/contracts/             @yegamble
